From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:20:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Draw the 3D view for each eye with a stereo preference

With "stereo 3D view" in the 3D view preferences, the preview widget asks
for stereo buffers and QGLView::paintGL() sets the eye offset from
currentTargetBuffer(), so the view is drawn once into the left buffer and
once into the right buffer from the same scene data. The eye separation is
a percentage of the distance to the point looked at and changes at once.
Picking and centering keep using the camera between the eyes. Qt before
6.5 has no currentTargetBuffer() and keeps the single view.

Assisted-by: glm-5.3:cloud (Ollama) via Codex
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
